---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <h1>About Visio Nova Mundi CIC</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Visio Nova Mundi CIC is a London-based social innovation organisation combining research,
    institutional reform, and applied pilot programmes to improve how systems serve people and communities.
  </p>

  <div class="grid">
    <section class="card">
      <h2>Mission</h2>
      <p>
        To strengthen institutions, improve public service delivery, and create sustainable models that expand opportunity and long-term wellbeing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Vision</h2>
      <p>
        A future where institutions operate ethically, effectively, and inclusively — ensuring communities have access to opportunity, wellbeing, and fair systems of support.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Values</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Integrity</strong> — transparency, ethics, accountability</li>
        <li><strong>Innovation</strong> — practical solutions for complex challenges</li>
        <li><strong>Equity</strong> — inclusion and fair access to opportunity</li>
        <li><strong>Collaboration</strong> — cross-sector partnerships</li>
        <li><strong>Sustainability</strong> — long-term, responsible models</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="card founder">
    <h2>Founder perspective</h2>
    <p><strong>Marcel Florin Banias · Founder and Director.</strong> <a href="https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/16947678/officers">View the official director record</a>.</p>
    <p>
      Visio Nova Mundi was founded by Marcel Florin, drawing on cross-sector experience across healthcare environments,
      custodial institutions, community organisations, and operational food systems. This perspective supports an evidence-led,
      practical approach to designing better systems and measurable outcomes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Florin's long-term professional direction is as a <strong>Strategic Transformation Adviser</strong>, developing
      practical, research-led support for organisations, communities and public institutions. This future advisory work
      will be developed through research, demonstration projects, partnerships and appropriate future engagements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card learning">
    <p class="eyebrow">Organisational learning</p>
    <h2>Learning to Support Communities — Making Every Contact Count</h2>
    <p>
      At Visio Nova Mundi CIC, we believe positive community change begins with listening, understanding and helping people find the right support.
    </p>
    <p>
      In October 2026, our founder and director, Marcel Florin Banias, completed Making Every Contact Count (MECC) training through the London Borough of Waltham Forest. The training introduced a practical approach to short, supportive conversations through three steps:
    </p>

    <ol class="mecc-steps">
      <li><strong>Ask</strong><span>Listen carefully and understand what matters to the person.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Advise</strong><span>Share relevant, appropriate information without judgement.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Assist</strong><span>Help the person find suitable information or support.</span></li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      The learning also covered recognising opportunities to support wellbeing and signposting people to appropriate services. Read more on the <a href="https://www.walthamforest.gov.uk/health-and-wellbeing/public-health-strategies-and-policies/making-every-contact-count">London Borough of Waltham Forest MECC page</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      This learning will help inform how we design and develop our community-focused initiatives.
    </p>

    <h3 class="application-heading">How we hope to apply the learning</h3>
    <div class="application-grid">
      <section class="application">
        <h4>Unity House Centres</h4>
        <p>Use welcoming conversations to listen for community needs and, where appropriate, direct people towards suitable support.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="application">
        <h4>Circular Justice</h4>
        <p>If future work involves community engagement, approach residents experiencing food insecurity or other everyday difficulties with respect and without judgement.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="application">
        <h4>Satul Conectat România</h4>
        <p>Explore how community information hubs could help residents identify and access useful services. The model remains proposed.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="application">
        <h4>Clandestinus Educational Games</h4>
        <p>Explore supportive communication and inclusive educational experiences. Project Clandestinus is an independent founder-led venture; specialist education and safeguarding requirements remain separate.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="application-note">
      These are intended applications as projects develop, not claims of services already delivered or outcomes measured.
    </p>
    <p class="scope-note">
      <strong>Training scope:</strong> MECC is awareness and communication training. It is not a clinical qualification, medical advice certification or specialist safeguarding accreditation, and the training alone does not establish operational safeguarding readiness.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card verify">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accountability</p>
    <h2>How to verify and work with us</h2>
    <p>Visio Nova Mundi operates as a Community Interest Company for public benefit. Our governance page explains the asset lock, separation of independent ventures and approach to transparent reporting.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/governance">Read governance and transparency</a><a class="btn" href="/contact">Contact the CIC</a></div>
  </section>

  <style>
    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 40px;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .lead {
      margin: 0 0 18px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
      font-size: 18px;
      max-width: 80ch;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 14px;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      align-items: start;
    }

    .card {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 16px;
      background: white;
      box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    }

    .card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: 16px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .card p,
    .card li {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .card ul {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 18px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .founder {
      margin-top: 14px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39, 99, 235, 0.05), rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.05));
    }

    .learning {
      margin-top: 14px;
      padding: clamp(18px, 3vw, 28px);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(39, 99, 235, 0.045), rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.075));
    }

    .learning > p:not(.eyebrow) {
      max-width: 82ch;
      margin: 12px 0 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }

    .learning > h2 {
      max-width: 30ch;
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: clamp(22px, 2.8vw, 30px);
      line-height: 1.2;
      letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    }

    .learning a {
      color: #075e58;
      font-weight: 650;
      text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
    }

    .mecc-steps {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .mecc-steps li {
      display: grid;
      gap: 4px;
      align-content: start;
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 13px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .mecc-steps strong {
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .application-heading {
      margin: 22px 0 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 18px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    .application-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    .application {
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 14px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    }

    .application h4 {
      margin: 0 0 6px;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .learning .application p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .learning > .application-note {
      margin-top: 14px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .learning > .scope-note {
      margin-top: 12px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      border-left: 3px solid #0f766e;
      border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.68);
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .verify { margin-top: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.78); }
    .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 8px; color: #0f766e; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .actions { display:flex; gap:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:16px; }
    .btn { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:11px 14px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:14px; background:white; color:var(--text); text-decoration:none; font-weight:800; }
    .btn.primary { border-color:rgba(37,99,235,.25); background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10)); }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .mecc-steps,
      .application-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
